Z||000002||four50four||01-17-2000||10:19 PM||||nice, but with only 200 ponies and 275 ft-lbs....||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||01-17-2000||11:16 PM||||   One advantage of this engine over a small block is that the intake and coolant necks would be on the right side of the engine. Also, is it possible that the block is aluminum?? Since this car was built to handle well, I'd assume they would want to reduce weight in the rear of the car. 200 hp is not all that impressive but 275 lbs of torque in a car that light would be a blast.  I'm also betting that these engines are cheap as dirt at the scrap yards.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||01-18-2000||12:56 AM||||Would be pretty neat with nitrous,and,yes I believe this motor is all aluminum. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||01-18-2000||08:45 AM||||The block in aluminum but the heads and exhaust manifold is cast iron. I wonder how the weight of this motor compairs to the 2.8? If you could get a set of aluminum heads and bump the compression to 10:1 and get a  camshaft with a little more lift, I'd bet you coud easily get 250 Hp and raise the torque to well over 300 ft lbs. Now, add a turbo...||||reg||11
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||01-18-2000||02:28 PM||||That motor also bolts right up to all Fiero trannys.||||reg||14
